{
  "unit": {
    "id": "7",
    "title": "How many?",
    "blurb": "Numbers one to ten with plural nouns",
    "intro": "Numbers from four to ten never change: _quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem_. Two and three do change: _duo, duae, duo_ (two) and _trēs, trēs, tria_ (three) match the gender of what is counted. After a number, the noun stays in the case the sentence needs: _trēs puerī in hortō sunt_ (three boys are in the garden). _quot?_ asks 'how many?'."
  },
